<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Treaty</p><h1 class="enc-title">Anglo-Siamese Treaty of 1909</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1909</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a> · Also known as Bangkok Treaty of 1909</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Anglo-Siamese Treaty of 1909 was an agreement signed in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bangkok">Bangkok</a> by which Siam transferred its claims over the northern Malay states of Kedah, Kelantan, Terengganu and Perlis to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/britain">Britain</a>. In return Britain gave up most of its extraterritorial rights in Siam and provided a loan for railway building. The treaty fixed most of the modern border between <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thailand">Thailand</a> and Malaysia.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/anglo-siamese-treaty-of-1909.jpg" alt="Anglo-Siamese Treaty of 1909" width="320" height="503" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Governments of the United Kingdom and Siam · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Treaty_between_the_United_Kingdom_and_Siam_(1909).pdf" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
